# playwright e2e artifacts (HO 379 crawler + HO 472 fit-finish harness)
test-results/
playwright-report/

# diagnostic scratch (HO 672). Probes default to TRACKED — 126 of the 154
# diagnostics already were, and the 28 that weren't produced six citations in
# SKILL/backlog/roadmap pointing at files that existed on one machine. This
# directory is the opt-in for a probe known to be disposable when it is written,
# and it is the ONLY place under scripts/ that git and tsc both skip: tsconfig
# excludes it too, so a throwaway can never red-light `typecheck` or `build`.
# The README is negated back in so the directory and its rule ship with the repo.
scripts/diagnostic/scratch/*
!scripts/diagnostic/scratch/README.md

# design artefacts (HO 696). Mocks default to TRACKED. At the HO 672 close this
# directory held 20 tracked and 13 untracked with no disposable location at all,
# so every mock not deliberately committed was simply loose — and four tracked
# files, one of them shipped source, cited a mock absent from a fresh clone. This
# is the opt-in for a mock known disposable when it is saved (a browser-download
# duplicate, an iteration superseded before it was ruled); nothing tracked may
# cite a file in here, and `npm run check:design-citations` reds if one does.
# A ruling record never goes here. README negated back in so the rule ships.
docs/design/scratch/*
!docs/design/scratch/README.md

# handoff docs (HO 604). These were already ignored per-machine via
# core.excludesFile (~/.gitignore_global), so they never reach the repo and a
# deploy never sees them. Repeating it HERE is what stops Tailwind reading them:
# the v4 scanner honours a repo .gitignore but NOT core.excludesFile, so on this
# machine it was compiling class names out of handoff PROSE — `text-[10px]`,
# and a literal `text-[length:var(--fs-N)]` off a line of spec text. Those rules
# existed only in local builds, never in the deployed bundle, which is the
# problem: the local build compiled from inputs the deploy does not have. This
# line restores build-input parity and makes a fresh clone behave like this
# machine without needing the global ignore.
docs/handoffs/
